{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1398748-what\u2019s-the-origin-of-the-bogatyri","id":1398748,"title":"What\u2019s the origin of the Bogatyri?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-25T03:30:40-07:00","id":1398748,"title":"What\u2019s the origin of the Bogatyri?","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bogatyri_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bogatyri_(VTM</a>)<br /> So Bogatyri are unknown creatures devoted to Eldest. I find something interesting in their stuff:<br /> <br /> 1. They claimed lineage from <b>Meru</b> (To be honest, the other places I see this mountain is in Kindred of the East, it is the headquarter of Ten Thousand Immortals).<br /> 2. Although they appeared mortal, the bogatyri were not kine, Lupine, or Cainites (Mind you, Meru is the Immortals\u2019 headquarter).<br /> 3. Metal refused to cut their unblemished skin, while stone and wood forswore never to bruise them.<br /> 4. Lambach saw someone of <i>indescribable purity</i> watching over the Eldest.<br /> <br /> So what\u2019s their origin? Do they really have connections with Wan Gui or Immortals? Or they ARE Immortals? Or they are just another kind of celestial mystical beasts? Do anyone know more about them? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-25-2020, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T04:20:05-07:00","id":13